WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.790
Since the 1950s, many species in the upper
ocean have shifted about 52 kilometres

2
00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:08.610
towards the poles every decade.

3
00:00:08.660 --> 00:00:12.570
On the seafloor, about
29 kilometres a decade.

4
00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:17.590
And since 2006, North-east Atlantic
mackerel have expanded their summer feeding

5
00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:22.170
migration west and north,
into waters south of Iceland.

6
00:00:22.220 --> 00:00:24.490
Why are species moving poleward?

7
00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:26.530
Overfishing near the equator?

8
00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:28.170
Reversed ocean currents?

9
00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:29.770
A search for mates?

10
00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:33.250
In this mission, you'll test the
evidence behind a shifting migration,

11
00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:37.490
and see why a cause must
be tested, not assumed.

12
00:00:37.540 --> 00:00:42.990
Then you'll compare how fast soil erodes
from farmland with how fast it forms.

13
00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:46.510
Your mission: explain why sea
creatures are heading for the poles,

14
00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:50.360
and what warming means for
life and farms on land.
